## Reviewer disagreements (not applied)
- Q16–Q20 are not a Malay heading error. The Korean source, which the checker compares, and the English file use the same body lines. Promoting them to headings changes the outline.
- The zero-width breaks are not a Malay-only leftover. The Korean columns contain the same U+200B count. Deleting them fails `blocks`. The spoken "dan …" lines were left for the same reason.
- Article 3's 10% label was wrong as a description of the domestic rate. Dropping the digit 10 was not done. The label now states the domestic 21% and keeps the treaty ceiling of 10%, which the column body already explains. 004's number count stayed equal.
- "lelaki" was not added to the 010 lead sentence. Row 8 is the headlines. Row 16's suggested lead does not say male, and the English lead does not either.
- Bare "saat" meaning "the moment of" (saat kematian, saat dividen, 1 saat, dari saat, setiap saat) is ordinary Malay, not the preposition the verdict describes. The suggested Article 197 sentence itself keeps "dari saat".
